    "answer": {
      "short": "Both methods are correct: Bob obtains $\\cos3\\theta=\\frac12$, while Mary obtains $\\sin3\\theta=-\\frac12$.\n\nBoth identities reduce the cubic to a trigonometric equation; retain three distinct values of $x$.",
      "worked": "Both methods are correct.\n\nWith Bob’s substitution $x=\\cos\\theta$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n8\\cos^3\\theta-6\\cos\\theta-1&=0\\\\\n2\\cos3\\theta-1&=0\\\\\n\\cos3\\theta&=\\frac12.\n\\end{align*}$$\nWith Mary’s substitution $x=\\sin\\theta$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n8\\sin^3\\theta-6\\sin\\theta-1&=0\\\\\n-2\\sin3\\theta-1&=0\\\\\n\\sin3\\theta&=-\\frac12.\n\\end{align*}$$\nBoth follow from the supplied identities and give the same three distinct polynomial roots. Mary must take care to discard repeated sine values and continue until all three roots have been found.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
